                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I used to play this game in Chrome a lot. Its a great way to relaxe! Simple, charming, and easy to play. The wonderful thing about it is, however, that the depth of strategy is pretty great. You need to try to build paths that give you lots of loops through other tiles, but dont force you into taking terminating paths to soon. There is nothing quite as satasfying as getting a really long path chained together. I highly recommend it if you like soothing puzzels that dont require a lot of fast actions, but do require you to plan ahead.\n\nThis game is a solid puzzle game, very relaxing, and addicting. It's a nice break from more fast paced games, or games that require you to time events. Just sit back, relax, and play some tiles. \n\nSide note: I got the steam copy free because I had paid for the premium version in Chrome. I dont think that taints my review, as I liked the game a lot before they gave me the free copy, but just want to be upfront. I'm actually pretty impressed they did that, does not seem to be the norm!\n\nUpdate: Just realized I needed to sign in with my google account... that... seems very odd for a steam game... I would appreciate it if the game was integrated with my steam account, as I am sure most steam users would too. The current set-up lacks elegance. I should not need to log in with an external account to post scores.",
